    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSmall holding in a very popular area outside Cavan Town\n\nA well-regarded parcel of 2.2 hectares (5.5 acres) in a sought-after setting on the outskirts of Cavan Town.\n\nLand at Drumbar presents an opportunity to acquire a compact but well-configured grassland holding in one of County Cavan's more consistently popular residential catchments. Extending to approximately 2.2 hectares (5.5 acres), the land is currently laid in grass and maintained in good order, with a gently sloping aspect that runs down to the L5537 local road, providing a clear and accessible road frontage.\n\nThe site benefits from a mature hedgerow boundary in part, which frames the perimeter and lends a degree of established character to the holding. The elevated nature of the ground produces open, far-reaching views across the surrounding Cavan countryside — a quality that would be an appreciable asset whether the land is retained in agricultural use or advanced through the planning process for residential development. \n\nThe holding is well suited to country lifestyle buyers, those with equestrian or smallholding interests, and prospective self-builders / developers / investors seeking a manageable site in an area close to the full services of Cavan Town. Prospective purchasers with an interest in the development potential of the site should satisfy themselves as to the applicable zoning and policy objectives within the current Cavan County Development Plan.\n\nViewing\nViewing to be organised with the sole agents Savills Country Agency.\n\nServices\nMains water connection. \nPlease be advised that the selling agents have not checked the services and any purchaser should satisfy themselves with the availability and adequacy of all services. \n\nOffers\nOffers may be submitted to the sole selling agents:\nSavills, 33 Molesworth Street, Dublin 2. \n\nWayleaves and Rights of Access \nThe property will be sold with the benefit of all existing wayleave rights, including rights of access and rights of way, whether public or private. The purchaser will be held to have satisfied themselves as to the nature of all such rights and others."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Attractive land parcel in a desirable area</li><li>Extensive road frontage with obvious future development potential (S.P.P.)</li><li>Suitable for a variety of uses including equestrian</li><li>Elevated site with far reaching countryside views</li><li>Located on the outskirts of Cavan town</ul>"
      },
